WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:00.960
Welcome.

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.480
Let's go ahead and move right into

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.720
step two of the setup process.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.320
In this step, we're going to choose

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:08.640
where your AI's memory actually lives.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:11.120
So Continuum creates just one folder.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.760
Inside of it goes the working copy of your conversations

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:16.160
as well as the constitution that's written from them.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.240
And don't worry, your original export

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.600
file isn't changed at all.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.160
That just remains a completely separate copy.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:25.760
Basically every layer lives inside this one single folder.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.920
That means your constitution, the findings it

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.320
was written from, and your searchable history.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:32.800
As for space, it needs about 1.2

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:34.720
times the size of your export file.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.240
You'll actually find your own specific

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:38.240
estimate right beside this explainer.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.080
Now it can live in two places.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:42.400
On this Mac is really the simple answer.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.800
It's just always there while you're using the computer, sitting

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:47.760
in a folder called Continuum right in your home folder.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:50.480
Honestly, that's the suggested choice for most people.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.280
An external drive, on the other hand, definitely saves space

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.960
on the Mac, but it does have to be plugged

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.520
in whenever your AI needs to access that history.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.520
If it happens to be unplugged, the assistant will

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.360
just tell you it can't reach the history.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.400
Nothing is lost.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:05.030
But wherever you end up putting it, just make

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:07.030
sure to pick a folder that stays put.

00:01:07.030 --> 00:01:09.030
You really don't want one that gets automatically

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.430
copied to a cloud service because the memory

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.430
needs to stay firmly in one place.

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:16.470
The assistant will actually check the location before continuing.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:18.390
And keep in mind the Continuum program

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.710
itself always stays right on the Mac.

00:01:20.710 --> 00:01:22.390
This choice we're making right now only

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:24.630
decides where the memory folder lives.

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.710
This Mac or an external drive.

